  "raw": {
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/105": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - SOM Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is seeking outstanding candidates interested in an academic emergency medicine faculty position. Our Department aims to be the premier academic department of emergency medicine—globally renowned for education, unrivaled patient-centered care, pioneering research, and developing the next generation of leaders in medicine. This faculty physician position offers numerous clinical and teaching opportunities within the Department, the University of Maryland School of Medicine (UMSOM), and the University of Maryland Medical Center (UMMC). All faculty teach a range of learners including medical students, resident and fellow physicians, and advanced practice providers. Emergency Medicine - Academic Opportunities in Baltimore, Maryland The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is seeking outstanding candidates interested in an academic emergency medicine faculty position. Our Department aims to be the premier academic department of emergency medicine—globally renowned for education, unrivaled patient-centered care, pioneering research, and developing the next generation of leaders in medicine. This faculty physician position offers numerous clinical and teaching opportunities within the Department, the University of Maryland School of Medicine (UMSOM), and the University of Maryland Medical Center (UMMC). All faculty teach a range of learners including medical students, resident and fellow physicians, and advanced practice providers. In addition, our Department maintains a strong focus on faculty development for physicians at every stage of their careers. Our highly respected team includes some of the most prominent voices in Emergency Medicine. We foster a sense of collaboration and mentorship by hosting faculty development workshops, sharing publishing opportunities, promoting speaking opportunities, and offering research support and guidance—especially to junior faculty. While rank and tenure status depend upon each candidate’s qualifications, the anticipated rank for new hires is Assistant Professor. Our Academic Organization: INSTITUTIONAL RESOURCES - Our Emergency Medicine physicians are faculty members of UMSOM, the first public medical school in the United States and one of the fastest-growing, top-tier biomedical research enterprises in the world. UMSOM generates nearly $600 million in research and development annually and consistently outpaces its peers in terms of medical research and education. In 2026, the National Science Foundation ranked UMSOM as 14 th among public medical schools. Ambitious academic physicians will appreciate the variety of interdisciplinary support and opportunities UMSOM offers, as well as its innovative medical school curriculum, which includes a required Emergency Medicine clerkship for all medical students. TEACHING - Our physicians are dedicated to educating residents and medical students every day—and ensuring their success as future physicians. From the classroom to the bedside, our clinical educators impart knowledge, teach skills, and equip learners with the leadership and clinical judgment necessary to diagnose illnesses and treat patients in some of the most complex, high-stakes environments in medicine. Whether leading a small group workshop or presenting at grand rounds, faculty physicians are empowered to teach—and do so much more. Opportunities abound for faculty to develop their own curricula, mentor physicians-in-training, and shape the future of medical education at UMSOM. RESIDENCY AND FELLOWSHIPS - Our categorical and combined Emergency Medicine residencies host more than 50 resident physicians. Our program is one of the nation’s largest and most student-centered programs in the nation. We are the only program in the country to offer training in four tracks: emergency medicine, emergency medicine/pediatrics, emergency medicine/internal medicine, and emergency medicine/internal medicine/critical care. We also offer fellowships in diverse areas from emergency cardiology to faculty development, point-of-care ultrasound, health policy, and simulation, among others. CLINICAL - Our academic practice staffs and manages Emergency Departments at four hospitals in the heart of downtown Baltimore: the University of Maryland Medical Center-Downtown Campus, the University of Maryland Medical Center-Midtown Campus, Mercy Medical Center, and the Baltimore Veterans Affairs Medical Center. These facilities are enriched with state-of-the-art technology—from point-of-care ultrasound to hyperbaric chambers, advanced radiological and airway equipment, comprehensive stroke centers, and much more. Our patient population is diverse, urban, and underserved; caring for our neighbors in Baltimore and the patients who trust us in their greatest times of need is our honor. RESEARCH - Our Emergency Medicine faculty are a diverse group of clinical, basic science, and epidemiologic investigators who have successfully obtained more than $16 million in grants and contracts since 2021. Our current research focuses on data analytics, health computing, critical care, clinical operations, carbon monoxide, sickle cell disease, and hyperbaric oxygen therapy. In the past year, our faculty have published peer-reviewed journal articles in Science Advances and The New England Journal of Medicine, in addition to a range of esteemed publications focused on emergency medicine, hyperbaric medicine, emergency medical services, population health, critical care, and other topics. Expected salary range for Assistant Professors is $260,000 (min) and $290,700 (max). The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range may not include all components of the Emergency Medicine faculty compensation program or pay from participation in departmental variable compensation programs. Annual performance bonus eligible (up to 15% of base salary). Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring manager. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. The University of Maryland School of Medicine (SOM) was chartered in 1807 as the first public medical school in the United States. It continues today as one of the fastest growing, top-tier biomedical research enterprises in the world. SOM is dedicated to providing excellence in biomedical education, basic and clinical research, quality patient care and service to improve the health of the citizens of Maryland and beyond. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible in Emergency Medicine The appointee should also show potential for superior teaching, service, and research, scholarship, or creative performance, commensurate with the mission of the institution."
    },
    "https://efzv.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1013/job/128": {
      "title": "Associate Professor - SOM Med Cardiology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: General Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Baltimore, MD, United States Academic Electrophysiologist (3-309-1234)-The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is recruiting an Electrophysiologist for its expanding Electrophysiology (EP) Program. Academic Electrophysiologist (3-309-1234)-The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine at the University of Maryland School of Medicine is recruiting an Electrophysiologist for its expanding Electrophysiology (EP) Program. The University of Maryland Health System represents a dynamic, regional cardiovascular network that spans the Baltimore and Washington DC capital region and ranks among the nation’s very best in cardiac care. This position will be appointed as a full-time faculty member at the University of Maryland School of Medicine. Expected faculty rank will be Assistant Professor or higher, however, final rank, tenure status and salary will be commensurate with the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. The expected salary range for Assistant Professors is $225,831 (min) and $650,000 (max). The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. This salary range does not include all components of the departmental faculty compensation program or pay from participation in departmental variable compensation programs. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on the University of Maryland School of Medicine’s good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. UMB offers a comprehensive benefits package that prioritizes wellness, work/life balance, and professional development. This position participates in a retirement program that must be selected and is effective on your date of hire. Faculty receive a generous leave package that includes over 4 weeks of vacation accrued each year, paid holidays, personal leave, unlimited accrual of sick time, and comprehensive health insurance; professional learning and development programs; tuition remission for employees and their dependents at any University System of Maryland school. You are also invited to view the Department of Medicine benefits for full-time faculty members. The University of Maryland School of Medicine (SOM) was chartered in 1807 as the first public medical school in the United States. It continues today as one of the fastest growing, top-tier biomedical research enterprises in the world. SOM is dedicated to providing excellence in biomedical education, basic and clinical research, quality patient care and service to improve the health of the citizens of Maryland and beyond. Successful candidates should have a medical degree from a recognized accredited domestic university (or foreign equivalent), be board eligible or board certified in Cardiac Electrophysiology, and eligible for an unrestricted license in the State of Maryland. In addition, a strong interest and experience in teaching and clinical activities and demonstrated experience in research is desired. Our service is active in all aspects of diagnostic and interventional electrophysiology, including complex ablation of VT and atrial arrhythmias, extractions, biventricular pacing, atrial appendage closures and innovative device therapy. Candidates will be expected to expand our clinical programs as well as to provide clinical care to patients at the University of Maryland Medical Center and EP outpatient clinics at its outreach locations. The appointee ordinarily shall have had successful experience in teaching and research, scholarship, or creative performance, and, when appropriate to the mission of the institution, be competent to offer graduate instruction and direct graduate research. There shall also be evidence of relevant and effective service to the institution, the community, and the profession."
    },
